<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n68941" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μόχθ-ος</span></b> , ὁ,
		= Homeric <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μόγος</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>toil, hardship, distress</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμφὶ δ᾽ ἀέθλῳ δῆριν ἔχειν καὶ μ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hes.
					<u>Sc.</u>
					306
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μόχθων ἀμπνοά, ἀμοιβά</span>,
				<i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>O.</u>
				8.7
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>N.</u>
				5.48
			</span></i>: freq. in Trag., <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ch.</u>
				921
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ph.</u>
				480
			</span></i>, etc.: also in pl., <i>toils, troubles, hardships</i>,
				<i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				541
			</span></i> (lyr.), etc.; of the <i>labours</i> of Heracles, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Tr.</u>
				1101
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				1170
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μ. τέκνων</span>
			<i>for</i> them, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Med.</u>
				1261
			</span></i> (lyr.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μόχθον ἀμφὶ
			πράγμασι</span> Epigr. ap. <i><span class="en">
				Aeschin.
				3.184
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀπελλείου μ. γραφίδος</span>,
			of a picture, <i><span class="en">
				<u>APl.</u>
				4.178
			</span></i> (Antip. Sid.).—Rare in early Prose (not in <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
			</span></i> or Oratt.), cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μ. καὶ ταλαιπωρίη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Democr.
					223
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐλευθέριοι μ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Smp.</u>
					2.4
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διὰ μόχθων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Cyr.</u>
					1.6.25
				</span></i>
			: freq. in <i><span class="en">LXX,
				<u>Ex.</u>18.8</span></i>, al.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κόπος καὶ μ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>1 Ep.Thess.</u>
					2.9
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μ.</span> implies
			<i>hardship</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πόνος</span>
			<i>work</i> (but <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μ.</span> is said to be
			Cret. for 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πόνος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AB</u>
					1096
				</span></i>
			).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
